\description{
Creates customisable biplots for Principal Component Analysis (PCA) using
only base R graphics. Supports \code{\link[stats:prcomp]{stats::prcomp()}}, \code{\link[stats:princomp]{stats::princomp()}},
\code{vegan::rda()} (unconstrained PCA), \code{survey::svyprcomp()}, \code{FactoMineR::PCA()},
\code{ade4::dudi.pca()}, and \code{psych::principal()} objects, as well as custom score
and loading matrices.
}
\section{Notes}{

\code{group}, \code{group2}, and \code{group3} preserve existing factor level order, so
setting \code{factor(x, levels = ...)} beforehand controls the order of legend
items as well as colour, symbol, and smallest-to-largest \code{group3} symbol
size mapping.
}

\section{Backwards Compatibility}{

\code{betterbiplot} 2.0.0 streamlined the v1.x argument list by grouping fine-grained
styling into \code{lab.args}, \code{var.args}, \code{ellipse.args} (or \code{chull.args}), and
\code{leg.args}, and replacing \code{pc1}/\code{pc2} with \code{pc = c(1, 2)}. Legacy v1.x
argument names (such as \code{col.v}, \code{whichv}, \code{expand}, \code{lab_rotation},
\code{angle}, \code{se}, \code{cex.leg}, \code{lpx}, \code{f1.a}, \code{pc1}, \code{pc2}) are still accepted
with a deprecation warning.
}

